WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:03.520
Generative AI is built to move fast and
make things

2
00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:06.000
up. The practice of law is built to do the

3
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:09.680
exact opposite. If a standard language
model invents a fake

4
00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:12.720
quote in a marketing email, it's a minor
embarrassment.

5
00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:15.440
If it hallucinates a single case citation
in a court

6
00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:19.040
filing, a practicing lawyer could face
professional ruin.

7
00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:22.640
This creates what is known as the
efficiency trust deficit.

8
00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:25.280
It is the massive gap between the raw
speed an

9
00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:28.160
AI offers and the actual level of trust a
lawyer

10
00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:29.760
can place in its output.

11
00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:32.880
Standard language models optimize for word
probability.

12
00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:36.560
In their architecture, factual truth is a
statistical side effect

13
00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:38.400
rather than a core requirement.

14
00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:42.080
To survive in a high-stakes legal
environment, an AI cannot

15
00:00:42.080 --> 00:00:44.480
be a boundless creative generator.

16
00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:47.520
It has to be strictly defined by its
constraints, by

17
00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:50.880
the exact things it is explicitly
forbidden from doing.

18
00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:54.720
In this profession, processing millions of
documents in seconds doesn't

19
00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:56.000
make you an asset.

20
00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:58.480
If those results can't be trusted in front
of a

21
00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:01.960
judge, it makes you a massive professional
liability.

22
00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:04.120
That is why Veritas was built.

23
00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:08.680
It is a specialized intelligence platform
engineered entirely around structural

24
00:01:08.680 --> 00:01:12.760
constraints, designed exclusively for the
Australian legal system.

25
00:01:12.760 --> 00:01:16.920
Standard chatbots group concepts by word
frequency, blind to legal

26
00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:21.640
reasoning. Veritas uses a Neo4j graph
database to plot verified

27
00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:23.720
relationships between case law.

28
00:01:23.720 --> 00:01:27.560
By analyzing a case's position within the
vertical court hierarchy,

29
00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:31.320
it evaluates precedent strength exactly
like a human judge.

30
00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:34.520
Every single piece of reasoning it
generates is then forcibly

31
00:01:34.520 --> 00:01:37.880
checked against the strict rules of the
Australian court hierarchy

32
00:01:37.880 --> 00:01:41.720
and formatted to exact AGLC4 citation
standards.

33
00:01:41.720 --> 00:01:45.640
By restricting the search parameters
entirely to relational, proven case

34
00:01:45.640 --> 00:01:48.040
law, the system removes the guesswork.

35
00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:52.120
It replaces mathematical probability with
verified legal precedent.

36
00:01:52.120 --> 00:01:54.760
But external research is only half the
problem.

37
00:01:54.880 --> 00:01:58.560
A truly viable legal AI system has to
guard internal

38
00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:02.400
client information just as fiercely as it
checks its citations.

39
00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:05.120
This requires strict matter segregation.

40
00:02:05.120 --> 00:02:08.800
Every client file is completely isolated
from the rest, ensuring

41
00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:11.760
details never cross-contaminate during
analysis.

42
00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:16.880
Before processing, an automatic conflict
detection protocol cryptographically verifies that

43
00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:20.000
no conflicting interests exist before
analysis begins.

44
00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:23.040
Once it starts, every single action the AI
takes is

45
00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:26.800
lolled. This creates an evidence chain of
custody, an unchangeable

46
00:02:26.800 --> 00:02:29.840
audit trail detailing exactly how the
platform arrived at its

47
00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:33.680
conclusion. That trail, along with all
associated data, is retained

48
00:02:33.680 --> 00:02:37.440
securely for exactly seven years, matching
the precise compliance requirements

49
00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:38.800
set by Australian law.

50
00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:42.960
Crucial features like end-to-end
encryption, strict segregation, and automatic conflict

51
00:02:42.960 --> 00:02:46.560
detection are often sold as premium
upgrades in enterprise software.

52
00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:50.360
But here inside the demanding legal field,
these features are

53
00:02:50.360 --> 00:02:55.880
the absolute non-negotiable minimums
required to avoid professional malpractice.

54
00:02:55.880 --> 00:02:59.320
The current trend in artificial
intelligence is to build models

55
00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:02.600
that know a little bit about absolutely
everything.

56
00:03:02.600 --> 00:03:07.480
But in a highly specialized profession,
generalized omniscience is practically

57
00:03:07.480 --> 00:03:11.640
useless. A one-size-fits-all approach
falls apart when you try to

58
00:03:11.640 --> 00:03:16.600
force a generalized US-centric product
onto a highly specific framework

59
00:03:16.600 --> 00:03:18.600
like the Australian legal system.

60
00:03:18.600 --> 00:03:22.840
The rules, the terminology, and the
hierarchy are entirely different.

61
00:03:22.840 --> 00:03:26.200
Real progress in this space requires
building from the ground

62
00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:31.240
up. It means engineering hyper-localized
systems that are deeply constrained

63
00:03:31.240 --> 00:03:34.680
by the specific laws of the jurisdiction
they operate in.

64
00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:38.440
A professional platform earns its value by
providing an immutable

65
00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:43.080
audit trail for every conclusion,
subordinating raw speed to verifiable

66
00:03:43.080 --> 00:03:44.120
proof.

